#!/usr/bin/python3
# sg-appimage -- AppImages a person downloaded, installed for them alone.
#
# An AppImage (Foo-x86_64.AppImage) is a Linux program in one file: a small
# ELF "runtime" with the program's files appended as a SquashFS image. Here
# it is installed the way the AppImage project suggests -- the file in
# ~/Applications (made if missing; File Explorer shows it) -- and Start lists
# it as any Linux app: a desktop entry in ~/.local/share/applications
# (appimage-<id>.desktop) and its icon in ~/.local/share/icons/hicolor,
# which sg-linuxapp64.exe turns into a Start entry, an Uninstall entry
# (Settings > Apps) and its .ico. No root, nothing system-wide.
#
#   sg-appimage info FILE [--out OUT]         what the file is (KEY value lines)
#   sg-appimage install [--move] FILE [--out OUT]
#                                             install it (or the newer version
#                                             of one installed: replaced)
#   sg-appimage uninstall DESKTOP-FILE|ID [--out OUT]
#   sg-appimage list                          the installed ones
#   sg-appimage run APPIMAGE [ARG...]         start one (the entries' Exec)
#
# The file is never run to install it: an AppImage is a stranger's program
# until the person starts it. What Start needs -- its desktop entry and its
# icon -- is read out of the SquashFS with unsquashfs (-o: past the runtime;
# -cat: one file, symbolic links resolved inside the image only), and every
# value taken from it is cleaned: the name and comment are plain text, the
# entry's command is ours ("sg-appimage run FILE"), of the image's own Exec
# line only its file/URL placeholder is kept. Type 1 AppImages (an ISO 9660
# image, before 2017) and other formats (DwarFS) are refused, saying so.
#
# Started from Start, an AppImage mounts itself with FUSE (libfuse2t64,
# fusermount from fuse3); where FUSE cannot be used, it is started with
# APPIMAGE_EXTRACT_AND_RUN=1 (it unpacks itself into /tmp instead).
#
# SG_APPIMAGE_DIR, XDG_DATA_HOME, SG_UNSQUASHFS and SG_APPIMAGE_FUSE (a
# path standing for /dev/fuse) point all of this elsewhere for the gate
# (test/appimage-check.sh); SG_MUTANT_* make the gate's mutants.
#
